WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.393
In the Project Hub, the First Steps card brings together its songs and interface theme.

00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:09.832
Open it here. The same card also offers Android export.

00:00:10.473 --> 00:00:15.772
The start screen is editable. Watch the title in the center as the text field changes.

00:00:15.872 --> 00:00:18.501
The player will see First Steps Studio.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.704
Music Selection groups songs into sets, with a checklist for each song.

00:00:23.804 --> 00:00:27.637
Opening Easy takes us straight to its playable chart in the Song Editor.

00:00:28.273 --> 00:00:32.397
Here the chart starts empty, with beat markers already in place.

00:00:32.497 --> 00:00:36.806
Auto-place turns those markers into notes the author can move on the timeline.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.404
Dragging this arc moves its two attached taps from three and four seconds to five and six.

00:00:42.504 --> 00:00:44.683
One undo restores all three.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.389
Chart Check counts clicks, holds and flicks, and looks for awkward patterns.

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:56.083
This Easy chart has thirty-two notes and no flagged issues.

00:00:56.707 --> 00:01:00.590
On Hard, the hold body has its own cyan stripe material.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:04.249
Watch the stripes turn with the ribbon as the timeline advances.

00:01:04.873 --> 00:01:09.242
Player Settings controls music volume, hit sounds and note speed.

00:01:09.342 --> 00:01:14.191
Open Calibrate to see where players tap along to four beats to measure their audio offset.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.074
One interface theme covers several player screens.

00:01:18.174 --> 00:01:22.622
Switch from the title to Results to see how Neon presents the score and judgments.

00:01:23.273 --> 00:01:27.142
Selecting Clean Light previews another design for the same project.

00:01:27.242 --> 00:01:30.361
The theme cards and the live screen sit side by side.

00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:33.746
The editor guide opens over the current page.

00:01:33.846 --> 00:01:38.654
Here it opens directly to Project Hub, with links to the other five workspaces.

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:44.370
Here is First Steps Studio on the Galaxy S21, with the title we edited.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.684
Tap to open song selection and choose a difficulty.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:51.151
The gear opens the project's settings on the phone.

00:01:51.251 --> 00:01:54.365
Return to song selection to start the Easy chart.

00:01:55.007 --> 00:01:58.825
This is the striped hold from the editor, now running on the phone.

00:01:58.925 --> 00:02:02.049
Its active head follows the bend across three lanes.

00:02:03.007 --> 00:02:07.220
Drop 3D places taps on the ground and raises arcs above the lanes.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.624
From this perspective you can see where the two paths cross.

00:02:11.273 --> 00:02:14.172
Circle replaces the lanes with a moving disk.

00:02:14.272 --> 00:02:18.151
Follow the curved notes to the judgment ring as the disk changes position.

00:02:18.773 --> 00:02:22.887
In Scan Line, notes stay on the page and the judgment line moves.

00:02:22.987 --> 00:02:25.341
A note is due when the line reaches it.

00:02:25.973 --> 00:02:30.357
This desktop test places six different note shapes on one scan page.

00:02:30.457 --> 00:02:34.491
Squares, circles and triangles can share the same hit time.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:38.369
Back on the phone, pausing freezes the playfield.

00:02:38.469 --> 00:02:41.873
The player can resume the song, retry it or leave.

00:02:42.507 --> 00:02:47.970
At the end of this run, the results screen totals the score, accuracy and maximum combo.

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:50.909
The judgment counts show how the run was scored.
